#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# arg_min

#% text
# `arg_min(f, x)` gives a point where `f` attains its global minimum; `arg_min(f, [x, y])` gives the list of coordinates.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is the point of `minimize(f, x)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A parabola:

#% cell
arg_min(x^2 + 2*x, x)
#% output
#= -1

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Two variables:

#% cell
arg_min(x^2 + y^2 - 2*x + 4*y, [x, y])
#% output
#= [1, -2]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The minimum value at that point:

#% cell
min_value(x^2 + 2*x, x)
#% output
#= -1

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `minimize`, `arg_max`, `min_value`
